WEBVTT

00:07:58.396 --> 00:08:03.156
WPR: Reshma, we have a question here
from a TED Member, they ask,

00:08:03.156 --> 00:08:06.076
"The pandemic has showed that women
do an extra shift of work,

00:08:06.116 --> 00:08:09.236
most of the heavy lifting at home,
and upon returning to work,

00:08:09.236 --> 00:08:12.516
playing the role of the emotional
aunt in the workplace.

00:08:12.556 --> 00:08:15.396
What should allyship look like now
in order to support women

00:08:15.436 --> 00:08:16.996
as we come out of the pandemic?"

00:08:16.996 --> 00:08:18.396
RS: Talk about unpaid labor.

00:08:18.436 --> 00:08:21.196
You know, what about all
the unpaid labor women do at work?

00:08:21.236 --> 00:08:23.876
Who organizes the Christmas party
or the Hanukkah party?

00:08:23.916 --> 00:08:28.036
Or the book clubs or the speakers
or the D and I sessions?

00:08:28.076 --> 00:08:34.316
It’s always women, women of color,
and we don’t get paid for that.